# Saved files stay readable

When the bytes already on disk would still mean the same thing, stop here. Do not look up the format.

A change to what an existing player file means raises `FORMAT` in `PlayerDataUpdater`. Change `SINCE` only in that case. The updater reads every earlier number, migrates that folder when it is opened, and then writes the current layout.

A breaking change in `BookSettings` still reads an old `bluerecipebook.json` and updates that file when it loads.

Confirm any format update with the user before writing it. Stop to confirm.